+# CI Triage RCA — Open Unified Pipeline failed on PR #1896/merge (Run #40617102546)
+
+- **Work order:** #1897 (P2-medium, handoff:coder, area:ci, repo:open) — claimed atomically via bridge `work_claim` GRANT_NEW 2026-10-28T01:52:58Z (agent `contributor-agent`, 30-min lease)
+- **Failed job:** `Tower TS Verification (typecheck + contract-safe tests)` — workflow **CI — Open Unified Pipeline**, head ref `1896/merge`
+- **PR under test:** #1896 — `fix(tower): truncateToolResult JSON-safe prune` (the #1882/#1895 defect-class fix: oversized tool results previously emitted unparseable byte-clipped JSON + UTF-8 mojibake)
+- **Lane:** PR-lane only. `main` is green (runs 40617562721 / 40617538332, 01:51–01:52Z, conclusion success). Board agents cannot push to another agent's bridge branch, so this artifact is the triage evidence + exact ready-to-apply fix for the PR author lane.
+
+## 1. Why the failing line was not visible from the tower
+
+`github_get_failed_logs` for the run returns a fixed tail window (last ~17 lines) which contained only `Post job cleanup` noise — the `##[error]` line falls out of the window because the job's failing step is followed by the always-run "Trigger Federation CI Watchdog on Failure" step. This is the same result-pruning blind spot the tower truncation work (#1882/#1895, PR #1896) addresses. For comparison, the same tool DID surface the real error for run 40617424728 (`_INDEX.md differs from the regenerated index (502 live scripts found)`) because that job has no post-failure step pushing the marker out of the window.
+
+## 2. Reproduction methodology (exact CI parity, zero credentials)
+
+The open repo is public, so the CI workspace was reconstructed byte-for-byte:
+
+1. Downloaded the exact merge ref tarball: `codeload.github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/tar.gz/refs/pull/1896/merge` (8,963,906 bytes).
+2. Node v24.22.1 (matches `setup-node@v5` node-version 24), `npm ci` in `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane` (lockfile from the merge ref).
+3. Replicated the composite action `./.github/actions/setup-node-tower` exactly: `npm run typecheck` → `tsc --noEmit`, then `npm run test:tower-ci`.
+
+## 3. Findings (each independently verified)
+
+| Check | Result on `1896/merge` | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|
+| `tsc --noEmit` (strict, ES2022, NodeNext, src/** only) | exit 0 | **NOT the failure** |
+| New suite `test_rate_limit_truncation.ts` (9 contract groups) | ALL 9 PASS | new truncation code is sound |
+| New suite `test_truncation_live_replay.ts` (triple-encoded 553,464-byte replay) | PASS (517,591 bytes emitted, mode json-prune, 0 mojibake, parseable at all 3 layers) | live defect genuinely fixed |
+| Full `npm run test:tower-ci` chain | **exit 1 at `test:wiring-guard`** | **THE failure** |
+
+The wiring guard's exact output (per #116 contract):
+
+```
+❌ wiring guard: 1 test file(s) referenced by NO npm script:
+   - test_session_admission.ts
+Wire each via scripts/test-runner.ts (direct or env-gated) per #116.
+```
+
+## 4. Root cause
+
+PR #1896 rewrote `src/lib/mcp_rate_limit.ts` (the JSON-safe prune, +134 lines) and added two new suites, wiring them into `test:unit` and `test:tower-ci`. In the same edit it **removed the `test:session-admission` script entry and both chain references from `package.json`** while leaving `test_session_admission.ts` in place (4,896 bytes, identical to main). The wiring guard (`scripts/test-runner.ts --guard`) fails the build when any root-level test file is referenced by no npm script, so the job died before/at the guard step.
+
+**The removal is unjustified:** `tsx test_session_admission.ts` on the PR tree passes **9/9 contract groups** (`test_session_admission: 9/9 contract groups PASS (#1886 pressure-eviction admission)`). The test guards merged behavior from PR #1894 (#1886 bounded /mcp session table pressure-eviction admission, merged 01:45Z) and is fully compatible with the new truncation code.
+
+## 5. Exact fix (3 wiring lines restored, byte-identical to `main`'s wiring)
+
+Apply to `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/package.json` on the PR branch:
+
+```diff
+--- a/infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/package.json  (refs/pull/1896/merge)
++++ b/infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/package.json
+@@ (scripts)
+     "test:mcp-presence": "tsx test_mcp_presence.ts",
++    "test:session-admission": "tsx test_session_admission.ts",
+     "test:bridge-intake": "tsx test_bridge_intake.ts",
+@@ (test:unit, after test:mcp-presence)
+-    ... && npm run test:mcp-presence && npm run test:policy && ...
++    ... && npm run test:mcp-presence && npm run test:session-admission && npm run test:policy && ...
+@@ (test:tower-ci, after test:mcp-presence)
+-    ... && npm run --silent test:mcp-presence && npm run --silent test:client-registry && ...
++    ... && npm run --silent test:mcp-presence && npm run --silent test:session-admission && npm run --silent test:client-registry && ...
+```
+
+The full machine-applicable unified diff is included in the bridge submission metadata; the three insertions restore `main`'s wiring exactly (position: `test:session-admission` between `test:mcp-presence` and `test:policy`/`test:client-registry`).
+
+## 6. Verification after fix
+
+Re-ran the full chain on the patched tree: `npm run test:tower-ci` → **exit 0** — every suite green including `test:wiring-guard` ("no unwired test files"), both new truncation suites, `test:session-admission` (9/9), task-engine, federation, semantic-router. `package.json` remains valid JSON. The new truncation behavior itself is proven good by the two new suites plus the replay test (553,464-byte triple-encoded fixture → 517,591 bytes valid JSON at all 3 layers, cap honored, zero U+FFFD).
+
+## 7. Handoff (PR author lane — single 3-line edit)
+
+1. Apply the diff in §5 to the PR branch (`bridge/bridge-20261028-tower-truncation-json-prune`), rebase on latest `main` (Dual-Rebase invariant), push.
+2. The `1896/merge` re-run should be fully green: typecheck already passes, wiring guard satisfied, both new suites pass.
+3. Do NOT delete `test_session_admission.ts` as an alternative "fix" — that would drop the #1886 pressure-eviction guard from CI and starve the suite (Superior Replacement invariant: fix the wiring, not the coverage).
+
